{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T20:10:47.139Z","author":"orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"259b6fa8d51ec5e6f7d340fb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/10","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-03T20:10:47.138Z","author":"orchestrator","text":"Orchestrator review (2026-11-03 20:40Z): the codex continuation hit its 6h timeout during the serial Bun gate, after the full npm release gate passed (19:08Z). The staged diff has no profiling hooks (no __pmProfile or PM_MEMORY_PROFILE). Every property budget stays at 500 seeds, and the seed ledger makes each suite prove 500 unique, correctly valued coordinates; the agent's mutation that drops coordinate 237 fails 499 !== 500. The CI matrix keeps the three complete gates as separate jobs, and the test (22) and test (26) required checks aggregate them, refusing failure, cancellation or skip. Local re-check: typecheck 0, lint 0, duplication 0%, the seed/worker-budget/release-ci tests 12/12, changelog current. The PR's CI must confirm the Bun gate and the duration target."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T20:10:47.139Z"}],"before_hash":"ec416b23a5af8c9e0117bff5a38d6ccd382fe6eaa5aa8d9aae6845314d6a61dd","after_hash":"3db6fc585339856770605e77f28092147ba22bf365b01b7ab15e264c9432d66f","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ae9aac001e8088c61e5e6f13745373cc10ebf914f250dd20471d87493ad157b2"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T21:41:22.774Z","author":"orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"259b6fa8d51ec5e6f7d340fb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/11","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-03T21:41:22.773Z","author":"orchestrator","text":"CodeRabbit round 1 on 81b3201, all four findings fixed. (1) Besides the aggregate needs.runtime.result, the test (22) and test (26) aggregators now read each runtime leg's conclusion through actions/runs/RUN_ID/jobs?filter=latest (actions: read), which also returns legs carried over by a re-run of failed jobs. They require exactly three legs and all success. A stand-in gh tests 3 success, 2 or 4 legs, cancelled, skipped, null and an API failure; removing the length check fails the test. (2) docs/property-suite-duration.md says the npm gate passed and the Bun gate's result and per-test durations are pending CI. (3) Worker slots record their owner PID and are reclaimed on EEXIST when process.kill(pid, 0) reports ESRCH; empty or unreadable files stay owned. (4) Pool lanes stop claiming batches once any lane has recorded a failure, like concurrentCases. A 12-batch pool with a failing first batch starts fewer than 12; without the stop it starts 12 of 12. Lint, typecheck, duplication and docstring pass; release-ci, worker-budget and property-seeds tests pass 15/15 under Node and 7/7 under Bun."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T21:41:22.774Z"}],"before_hash":"3db6fc585339856770605e77f28092147ba22bf365b01b7ab15e264c9432d66f","after_hash":"1fee918d99d3c74d9b02f2758ce215d7573080c271de1e86e7e385be06eecb8c","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d6eebae6c83896113de65936fd637e644719f4fbdb74406ac62ace93ec42088c"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T22:34:57.487Z","author":"orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"259b6fa8d51ec5e6f7d340fb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/12","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-03T22:34:57.487Z","author":"orchestrator","text":"CodeRabbit round 2 on f3884fd: if writing the owner PID into a newly claimed slot failed, the handle stayed open and an empty claim that ownerIsGone() never reclaims stayed behind. The PID write now closes the handle in finally and removes the claim before rethrowing. The success path is unchanged; worker-budget passes 4/4 under Node and Bun, and lint, typecheck and duplication pass. No test forces the write to fail: that needs a filesystem fault, and the code is three lines."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T22:34:57.487Z"}],"before_hash":"1fee918d99d3c74d9b02f2758ce215d7573080c271de1e86e7e385be06eecb8c","after_hash":"a3a9aef4d9f44cb93affcc46c9cb7327f637a5f6f9d2095cf6f675af6c7a5189","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"58af48d723b51afdb7ef5cafe540d6411c07ca691d61a3461741bc31674daeac"}
